# Admin/control-plane rules — HIGH SECURITY

Admin is a separate privileged security boundary, not merely another consumer page.

## Architecture
- Prefer a separate admin app/hostname and separate privileged API boundary where practical.
- Do not expose admin navigation/routes in consumer UI.
- Hidden URL is not a security control; assume attackers can discover the hostname/path.
- Infrastructure access restrictions (Cloudflare Access/VPN/Tailscale/IP policy) are recommended defense-in-depth.

## Authorization
- Default deny. No privileged action without explicit server-side permission.
- Do not authorize with `email === ownerEmail` alone.
- Model roles/permissions explicitly (`OWNER`, future support/ops roles) with least privilege.
- Owner/admin identities require mandatory strong MFA/passkey/TOTP.
- Consider distinct privileged/admin session context from normal consumer session.
- Sensitive actions require recent re-authentication/step-up verification.

## Dangerous actions
Examples: usage adjustment, refund, model enable/disable, feature flag, admin grant, user ban, global AI kill switch.
- Validate input strictly.
- Require explicit permission.
- Record append-only admin audit event with actor, action, target, request ID, time and reason/result.
- Prefer reversible/config-versioned changes where possible.

## Visibility/privacy
- Admin APIs must not leak user secrets/passwords/session tokens/provider keys.
- Views should minimize personal data and require a legitimate operational purpose.
- Production must not register local/mock admin shortcuts.
